# The designer's helper CLI splices bytes into *-designer.go and writes LF,
# and gofmt normalises the whole file to LF whenever it rewrites one. A
# checkout with CRLF would therefore turn every designer edit into a mixed-
# ending file and a whole-file diff, so the working tree is LF on every
# platform - Go, gofmt and the Go toolchain are all fine with that on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.vsix binary
*.exe binary
